# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local provider plugin cache and module cache. Machine-specific, large,
# and fully reproducible from `terraform init`. Never commit.
**/.terraform/*
**/.terraform

# State files. These are the single most dangerous thing you can commit:
# Terraform state stores every attribute of every resource IN PLAINTEXT,
# including generated passwords, connection strings, certificates and keys.
# State belongs in the remote backend (Azure Storage, RBAC-restricted), not git.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup

# Crash logs produced when Terraform or a provider panics.
crash.log
crash.*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Variable files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.tfvars commonly hold environment-specific values and occasionally secrets.
# We ignore them by default and whitelist the ones that are deliberately
# committed:
#   - envs/*/terraform.tfvars  -> checked in on purpose; they contain only
#     non-sensitive environment shape (node counts, SKUs, CIDRs). Secrets are
#     never placed there; they come from Key Vault or OIDC-issued tokens.
#   - *.auto.tfvars.example / *.tfvars.example -> templates for humans.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
!*.auto.tfvars.example
!envs/*/terraform.tfvars

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend.hcl holds the storage account / resource group names of the state
# backend. Not strictly secret, but environment-specific and bootstrap-derived,
# so each operator generates their own. The .example file is committed.
backend.hcl
*.backend.hcl
!backend.hcl.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Plan artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A saved plan file is a serialised copy of the state delta and CAN contain
# sensitive values. Treat it like state: never commit, short retention in CI.
*.tfplan
tfplan
tfplan.json
tfdestroy
plan.txt
plan.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform lock files -- NOT IGNORED, DELIBERATELY COMMITTED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .terraform.lock.hcl records the exact provider versions AND their checksums
# for each platform. Committing it is the Terraform equivalent of committing
# package-lock.json:
#   1. Reproducibility   - every developer and every CI run resolves the exact
#                          same provider builds, so "works on my machine" and
#                          surprise provider upgrades disappear.
#   2. Supply-chain      - the recorded H1 hashes are verified on `init`,
#                          so a tampered or substituted provider binary fails.
#   3. Reviewable        - a provider bump becomes an explicit, diffable change
#                          in a pull request instead of an invisible event.
# Regenerate for all CI platforms with:
#   terraform providers lock -platform=windows_amd64 -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64
# (Do NOT add .terraform.lock.hcl below. The absence of an ignore rule is the point.)

# Terraform CLI config / credentials -- these DO contain tokens.
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
.terraform.d/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud / tooling credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.azure/
azureProfile.json
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
!**/testdata/**/*.pem
credentials.json
sp.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Kubeconfigs contain cluster credentials.
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig
.kube/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.infracost/
infracost.json
infracost-base.json
checkov-report.*
results.sarif
*.sarif
.tflint.d/
tflint-report.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json.example
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
*.bak
*.orig
*.log
!docs/**/*.log
